About the Opportunity  
 We are looking for a motivated, detail-oriented, and analytical Excellence Specialist to join our AFC Operations team. This entry-level role provides crucial support in monitoring performance metrics, maintaining operational documentation, and assisting in process optimization initiatives across Fraud, Sanctions, and Financial Crime operations. 
 This is an ideal opportunity for a junior professional looking to kickstart their career in fintech operations and financial crime compliance, working alongside experienced leaders to drive operational consistency and data accuracy. 
 &nbsp; 
 In This Role, You Will: &nbsp; 
 📊  Performance &amp; Data Support  


 Assist in gathering, updating, and compiling weekly/monthly AFC operational performance metrics (KPIs, SLAs). 


 Support the preparation of routine performance packs, dashboards, and review presentations for leadership. 


 Perform basic data checks to maintain high data accuracy in reporting routines. &nbsp; 


  ⚙️ Operational Support &amp; Process Maintenance  


 Assist in tracking operational workflows and maintaining clear Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). 


 Support senior specialists in executing continuous improvement deep-dives and routine process updates. 


 Log operational feedback and track follow-ups across teams. &nbsp; 


 📈  Workforce &amp; Resource Tracking  


 Help maintain baseline workforce tracking files and schedule logs in collaboration with operational leads. 


 Provide data inputs to support workforce management and capacity planning discussions. &nbsp; 


 🤝  Governance &amp; Coordination  


 Support administrative coordination for governance forums, preparing materials and tracking action items. 


 Assist in organizing audit readiness documentation and archiving control records. 


 Serve as a reliable operational interface for daily task follow-ups across AFC teams. &nbsp; 


 Profile Requirements 


 Experience: 0–2 years of relevant experience or internships in business operations, banking/fintech, analytics, or process support. 


 Skills: Solid foundation in Excel / Google Sheets; eagerness to learn data tools (SQL, Looker, Tableau) is a plus. 


 Mindset: High attention to detail, strong problem-solving mindset, organized, and proactive. 


 Communication: Strong verbal and written English communication skills; comfortable interacting with international cross-functional teams. 


 Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Economics, Finance, Engineering, or a related field. 


 &nbsp; 
 What’s in it for you 


 Accelerate your career growth by joining one of Europe’s most talked about disruptors . 


 Employee benefits that range from a competitive personal development budget, work from home budget, discounts to fitness &amp; wellness memberships, language apps and public transportation.&nbsp; 


 As an N26 employee you will have access to a Premium subscription on your personal N26 bank account. As well as subscriptions for friends and family members.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 


 Vacation days vary depending on your location of work. Additional day of annual leave for each year of service.&nbsp;&nbsp; 


 A high degree of autonomy and access to cutting edge technologies - all while working with a friendly team of peers of diverse nationalities, life experiences and family statuses.&nbsp; 


 A relocation package with visa support for those who need it. 


 &nbsp; 
 Who we are 
 N26 has reimagined banking for today’s digital world. Technology and design empower everything we do and it’s how we are building the global banking platform the world loves to use. 
